The public tests cover exact literals and independent small-integer/fraction oracles, Kahan capacity and refusals, ledger boundaries, original occurrence sharing, deterministic snapshots, UTF-8 transaction rollback, foreign/forward references, scope and sort refusals, required receipts, generated provenance, simultaneous substitution, lifting under a binder, bound instantiation, permanent storage limits, partial expressions beneath zero, explicit contradictory hypotheses and every operator variant. The proof fixtures additionally cover exact field schemas, conditional and assumed cancellation, retained partial operands, supplied product/quotient/power derivative premises, Jacobian ordering, simultaneous guard substitution, exact expected claims, every wire truncation, changed semantic versions, forward references, strict shortcut improvement and proof/byte/replay/coefficient ceilings. An independently assembled 401-byte v3 cancellation fixture checks the encoder separately from the decoder. New generator fixtures cover derivative laws, strict domains, the pendulum model, deterministic responses, frozen costs, changed policies, shortcut reuse, queue quotas and resource/support dominance. Tiny frozen graphs are compared with complete simple-path enumeration. No existing algebra or units implementation or tests supply these fixtures.

